{title: 080 - O World of God}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #080 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 80}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]O world [A]of God, [G/B]so vast [A7/G]and strange,
[A7]profound and wonderful [Em]and fair,
[D]Beyond [Bm]the [D]utmost [Bm]reach of thought,
[Bm]but not beyond [F#m]a Father's care!
[Em]We [A/E]are [Em]not strangers [A]on this [Em]earth
[Em]whirling amid [A]the suns of space;
[Bm]We are [A7]God's [G]children, [D]this [A7/C#]our home,
[D/A]with those of [A7]every [Bm/F#]clime and [Em]race.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]O world [A]of man [G/B]where life [A7/G]is lived,
[A7]so strangely mingling [Em]joy and pain,
[D]So [Bm]full [D]of evil [Bm]and of good,
[Bm]so needful [F#m]that the good shall reign!
[Em]It [A/E]is [Em]this world [F#m]that [A]God has [Em]loved,
[Em]and goodness was [A]its Maker's plan,
[Bm]The promise [G]of [D]God's [A7/C#]triumph is
[D/A]His coming [A7]in a [Bm/F#]Son of [Em]Man.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]O world [A]of time's [G/B]farstretching [A7/G]years!
[A7]there was a day when time [Em]stood still,
[D]A [Bm]central [D/A]moment [Bm]when there rose
[Bm]across upon [F#m]a cruel hill;
[Em]In [A/E]pain [Em]and death [F#m]love's [A]power [Em]was seen,
[Em]the mystery [A]of time revealed,
[Bm]The wisdom [G]of [D]the ways [A7/C#]of God,
[D/A]the grace through [A7]which man's [Bm/F#]hurt is [Em]healed.
{end_of_verse}
